While on the Oracle level, playing as an elven ranger I foolishly
pushed a boulder through a doorway into a corridors which went
sharp left immediately after the door.  This meant that I
couldn't get my character through the doorway as he would have
had to have moved diagonally.  Unfortunately this blocked my path
to leave the level, both to go down to the next level or up to
the previous.

I tried reading a scroll of teleportation but unfortunately that
didn't take me past the obstruction - I didn't have teleportation
control.  I didn't have any weapons or tools with which to
shatter the boulder and my only spell was Slow Monster (with a
100% failure rate).

Can anyone think of a way out of this situation?

As it happened, a little later my ranger was killed by a pack of
rothes after a singularly unfortunate patch of bad luck with
arrows which failed to find their target (damn the RNG!)

